---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_210",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 210,
  "text": "[[814.4]] <b>172.  Demonstratio axiomatum de identitate ac diversitate [April bis Oktober 1686 (?)]</b>\n [[814.5]] <tab/>[April bis Oktober 1686 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[814.22]] 1) Si sit propositio vera, in quam ingreditur ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> et pro ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> substituendo ^&.za <Leibniz special character> caeteris\n[[814.23]] omnibus manentibus fiat propositio falsa; dicetur ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> et ^&.za <Leibniz special character> <b>discerni</b>. </p>\n<p> [[814.24]] 2) Si ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> et ^&.za <Leibniz special character> possunt discerni, dicuntur <b>diversa</b>. </p>\n<p> [[814.25]] 3) Si ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> et ^&.za <Leibniz special character> non possunt discerni dicuntur <b>eadem</b>. </p>\n<p> [[814.26]] 4) Quae non sunt eadem ea sunt diversa. </p>\n<p> [[814.27]] 5) Quae eadem esse colliguntur, dicimus <b>Coincidentia</b>, exempli causa si duae\n[[814.28]] sint rectae quarum quaelibet circulum bisecat, ostendi potest medium punctum unius\n[[815.1]] idem esse cum medio puncto alterius, ideo dicemus media diametrorum circuli puncta\n[[815.2]] coincidere. </p>\n<p> [[815.3]] 6) ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> et ^&.za <Leibniz special character> esse <b>eadem</b>, ita designo: ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> ^&.za <Leibniz special character>, </p>\n<p> [[815.4]] 7) <b>diversa</b> vero ita: ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> non ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> ^&.za <Leibniz special character> </p>\n<p> [[815.5]] 8) Quae eadem sunt, eorum unum alteri substitui potest salva veritate, </p>\n<p> [[815.6]] (1) Sit ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> ^&.za <Leibniz special character>. </p>\n<p> [[815.7]] (2) Et sit propositio vera ^&.zi <Leibniz special character> </p>\n<p> [[815.8]] (3) in qua ^&.SD <Leibniz special character>. </p>\n<p> [[815.9]] (4) Dico si in ^&.zi <Leibniz special character> pro ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> ponas ^&.za <Leibniz special character> caeteris manentibus </p>\n<p> [[815.10]] (5) tunc fieri ^&.zh <Leibniz special character> veram. </p>\n<p> [[815.11]] (6) Nam alioqui ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> et ^&.za <Leibniz special character> discernentur (per prop. 1). </p>\n<p> [[815.12]] (7) Ergo non sunt eadem (per prop. 3) quod est contra hypothesin (hic 1). </p>\n<p> [[815.13]] 9) Quae eadem sunt uni tertio eadem sunt inter se. </p>\n<p> [[815.14]] (1) Sit ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> ^&.za <Leibniz special character> </p>\n<p> [[815.15]] (2) et ^&.za <Leibniz special character> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> ^&.zi <Leibniz special character>. </p>\n<p> [[815.16]] (3) Dico esse ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> ^&.zi <Leibniz special character>. </p>\n<p> [[815.17]] (4) Nam in art. 2 vero (ex hyp.) poni potest ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> pro ^&.za <Leibniz special character> ut fiat vera (per prop. 8) </p>\n<p> [[815.18]] (5) fit autem ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> ^&.zi <Leibniz special character> (per autopsiam ipsius 2). </p>\n<p> [[815.19]] (6) Ergo ^&.SD <Leibniz special character> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> [^&.zi <Leibniz special character>] vera (per 4 et 5) Q. E. D. (per 3). </p>\n<p> [[815.20]] 10) Quod diverso ab alio idem est, ab illo alio diversum est. </p>\n<p> [[815.21]] (1) <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> </p>\n<p> [[815.22]] (2) et <i>B</i> non ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> </p>\n<p> [[815.23]] (3) dico fore <i>A</i> non ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> </p>\n<p> [[815.24]] (4) Nam si <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i> erit (per artic. 1. hic et per prop. 9) <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>C</i>. </p>\n<p> [[815.25]] (5) quod est contra hyp. (art. 2). </p>\n",
  "number": "172.",
  "title": "Demonstratio axiomatum de identitate ac diversitate",
  "date": "[April bis Oktober 1686 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:172. Demonstratio axiomatum de identitate ac diversitate [April bis Oktober 1686 (?)] [April bis Oktober 1686 (?)] 1) Si sit propositio vera, in quam ingreditur ^&.SD et pro ^&.SD substituendo ^&.za caeteris omnibus manentibus fiat propositio falsa; dicetur ^&.SD et ^&.za discerni. 2) Si ^&.SD et ^&...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>